WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.833
Good to see you, Don.

00:00:00.833 --> 00:00:01.666
How are you?

00:00:01.666 --> 00:00:02.499
What's goin' on, Conan?

00:00:02.499 --> 00:00:03.504
I didn't see you, man.

00:00:03.504 --> 00:00:04.337
How are you?
[Conan] I'm good.

00:00:04.337 --> 00:00:06.670
I like that you were making fun of my hair

00:00:06.670 --> 00:00:08.940
just before we got started,

00:00:08.940 --> 00:00:11.463
'cause it's outta control and I apologize.

00:00:12.640 --> 00:00:14.270
No, no, no, I mean, I think your hair

00:00:14.270 --> 00:00:17.760
is taking care of all of the
making fun on all its own.

00:00:17.760 --> 00:00:18.840
I mean, especially this lick

00:00:18.840 --> 00:00:20.309
that you have going right now.

00:00:20.309 --> 00:00:21.153
Look at this, look at this.

00:00:21.153 --> 00:00:22.520
I can't--

00:00:22.520 --> 00:00:23.353
Look at that!

00:00:23.353 --> 00:00:26.020
See that's like a WiFi
antenna right there.

00:00:26.020 --> 00:00:29.670
I'm getting 5G right now, look at that.

00:00:29.670 --> 00:00:31.220
Look at that, I look like the little girl

00:00:31.220 --> 00:00:34.310
in the Dr. Seuss cartoon who wakes up

00:00:34.310 --> 00:00:35.560
when the Grinch is there.

00:00:36.890 --> 00:00:39.767
You said, you showed me just
before the show you've been,

00:00:39.767 --> 00:00:41.610
you went with--

00:00:41.610 --> 00:00:43.430
Wow, look at that.

00:00:43.430 --> 00:00:45.095
Braids, fantastic.

00:00:45.095 --> 00:00:46.130
Mama's (indistinct).

00:00:46.130 --> 00:00:47.863
Yeah, that's fantastic.

00:00:48.850 --> 00:00:50.240
Will you help me (laughs)?

00:00:50.240 --> 00:00:51.220
Please help.

00:00:51.220 --> 00:00:53.300
I would love to virtually
give you some help,

00:00:53.300 --> 00:00:56.620
but I think you gotta go
back to those hair shops

00:00:56.620 --> 00:00:57.720
and let them handle that.

00:00:57.720 --> 00:00:59.490
Yeah, yeah, yeah, I had this done once.

00:00:59.490 --> 00:01:02.833
I was up when we did a week of
shows at the Apollo Theater,

00:01:04.080 --> 00:01:05.760
some women there I went into their shop,

00:01:05.760 --> 00:01:06.880
and they braided my hair,

00:01:06.880 --> 00:01:10.404
and I've never felt pain
like that in my life.

00:01:10.404 --> 00:01:14.593
In my life, I have mad respect
for people that can do that.

00:01:15.706 --> 00:01:18.170
It gives you a natural face lift.

00:01:18.170 --> 00:01:19.880
It just pulls everything up.

00:01:19.880 --> 00:01:24.586
Yes, I did look like I was
sort of in my late 20s.

00:01:24.586 --> 00:01:29.280
But I was in constant pain,
so I'm never doing that again.

00:01:29.280 --> 00:01:32.890
Let me ask you how are you as a person?

00:01:32.890 --> 00:01:36.580
We'll get into you have I know
35 things going on right now,

00:01:36.580 --> 00:01:39.460
different projects, you always
do, you're a very busy guy,

00:01:39.460 --> 00:01:42.200
but how are you doing, how's your family?

00:01:42.200 --> 00:01:44.322
We're good for the most part.

00:01:44.322 --> 00:01:47.020
I'm very fortunate that, like I said,

00:01:47.020 --> 00:01:48.990
I live with someone who isn't sick of me,

00:01:48.990 --> 00:01:51.390
and we gotta have our routine,

00:01:51.390 --> 00:01:53.460
and we're here with the
dogs, and they're fine.

00:01:53.460 --> 00:01:56.270
Our kids have been outta
the house for a year now.

00:01:56.270 --> 00:02:00.350
And they're living together
actually not too far away,

00:02:00.350 --> 00:02:01.360
so we get to see them.

00:02:01.360 --> 00:02:03.510
They're like our COVID partners,

00:02:03.510 --> 00:02:04.950
you know, we get to go
over there and hang out.

00:02:04.950 --> 00:02:05.783
It's cool, it's cool.

00:02:05.783 --> 00:02:08.810
So your kids are old enough
to be living out on their own.

00:02:08.810 --> 00:02:09.990
Yeah, they're in their 20s now,

00:02:09.990 --> 00:02:12.740
so even if they didn't wanna
go, I was like, "You gotta go."

00:02:12.740 --> 00:02:13.710
So they're out.

00:02:13.710 --> 00:02:16.290
My kids are still very
young, but I made them leave.

00:02:16.290 --> 00:02:20.640
I just, I gave them each $120

00:02:20.640 --> 00:02:23.210
and I said, "I'll see you in a month."

00:02:23.210 --> 00:02:24.670
I think that's good parenting,

00:02:24.670 --> 00:02:27.930
because at times like this
when things are very tough

00:02:27.930 --> 00:02:29.950
where are they gonna
learn how to toughen up

00:02:29.950 --> 00:02:31.660
unless you kick them outta the nest

00:02:31.660 --> 00:02:34.200
and make them fend for
themselves like any good Dad?

00:02:34.200 --> 00:02:35.880
Yes, I thought it was tough love.

00:02:35.880 --> 00:02:36.713
I've had some people say,

00:02:36.713 --> 00:02:38.409
"You coulda given them more than 120 each

00:02:38.409 --> 00:02:40.420
and they seem pretty young."

00:02:40.420 --> 00:02:43.993
I don't think people should
tell me how to run my life.

00:02:45.160 --> 00:02:47.782
When I woke up we stilled
lived in America, right?

00:02:47.782 --> 00:02:48.976
Thank you!

00:02:48.976 --> 00:02:49.809
Thank you!

00:02:50.704 --> 00:02:53.180
(both laughing)

00:02:53.180 --> 00:02:55.313
Thank you, finally someone who gets it.

